<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lower Austria</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> is the largest state of Austria, lying in the north-east of the country around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>, which was long its capital; St. Pölten replaced it in 1986. The region formed the heart of the medieval duchy of Austria under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-babenberg">Babenbergs</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matthias-corvinus">Matthias Corvinus</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> occupied much of it, together with Vienna, from 1485 until his death in 1490.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lower-austria.jpg" alt="Lower Austria" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Written by Jon Harald Søby and Gryffindor; colours and ratio adjusted by User:Mevsfotw. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Lower_Austria.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
